      },
      {
        "label": "(ii) AU below-ladder sector bias",
        "text": "K1171 (N=13) adding AU drops primary \u03c1 from 0.441 \u2192 0.385. AU sits at inst_pct\u22480.37 (mid-high ladder) but \u03b8_rel=0.15 (very low, near-developed). Drop-AU LOO recovers K1172 \u03c1=0.441. AU is a mild leverage point attributable to ASX Top 10 being heavy on banks/miners whose earnings reports generate less idiosyncratic volatility than in US/CA/BR."
      },
      {
        "label": "(iii) K1163 EU cluster robust under full 30/30 coverage",
